1 AUTHORIZE

   Makes and changes the accounts in govax's authorization file, its
   SYSUAF.DAT: a JSON file on the host, ~/.govax/sysuaf.json unless the
   configuration key vax.authorization.file names another.  AUTHORIZE
   alone prompts UAF> for commands until EXIT or Ctrl/Z; with a command
   it runs that one.  MCR AUTHORIZE and RUN SYS$SYSTEM:AUTHORIZE are the
   same.  In a command procedure a session reads its commands from the
   data lines after it.

   Format

     AUTHORIZE [command]

2 Parameter

 command

   One of AUTHORIZE's commands, with its parameters and qualifiers.
   Without one, AUTHORIZE prompts for them.

2 Description

   The file is protected as VMS protects SYSUAF.DAT: owned by [1,4],
   (S:RWE,O:RWE,G,W).  A process in a system group, or with SYSPRV or
   BYPASS, may use it; others get %UAF-E-NAOFIL.

   A session ends with a message for each of the two parts of the file,
   the accounts (DONEMSG or NOMODS) and the rights database (RDBDONEMSG
   or RDBNOMODS).  One command prints only its own messages, and leaves
   $STATUS as VMS's AUTHORIZE did.

   The commands are:

     ADD username        A new account, a copy of DEFAULT's record with
                         the qualifiers' fields, and an identifier for
                         its UIC
     COPY old new        A new account, a copy of another's
     DEFAULT             Change the DEFAULT record new accounts copy
     MODIFY username     Change accounts; % and * match several
     REMOVE username     Delete an account and its UIC identifier
     RENAME old new      Change an account's username
     EXIT                End the session

   SHOW, LIST, and the identifier commands are still to come.

2 Qualifiers

   ADD, COPY, MODIFY, and DEFAULT take the fields of an account:

     /ACCOUNT=name       /ASTLM=n            /BIOLM=n
     /BYTLM=n            /CLI=name           /CLITABLES=name
     /CPUTIME=delta      /DEFPRIVILEGES=(..) /DEVICE=device
     /DIOLM=n            /DIRECTORY=[dir]    /ENQLM=n
     /FILLM=n            /FLAGS=(..)         /JTQUOTA=n
     /LGICMD=file        /MAXACCTJOBS=n      /MAXDETACH=n
     /MAXJOBS=n          /OWNER="name"       /[NO]PASSWORD=text
     /PBYTLM=n           /PGFLQUOTA=n        /PRCLM=n
     /PRIORITY=n         /PRIVILEGES=(..)    /QUEPRIO=n
     /SHRFILLM=n         /TQELM=n            /UIC=[group,member]
     /WSDEFAULT=n        /WSEXTENT=n         /WSQUOTA=n

   A UIC's numbers are octal.  /FLAGS and the privilege lists name what
   they set, and NO before a name clears it (/FLAGS=NODISUSER,
   /PRIVILEGES=(NOALL,TMPMBX)).  Of the flags only DISUSER does anything
   yet: it refuses a login.  govax keeps no login times, password
   lifetimes, or expiration dates, so /ACCESS, /PRIMEDAYS,
   /PWDLIFETIME, /PWDMINIMUM, /PWDEXPIRED, /EXPIRATION, and
   /GENERATE_PASSWORD are not accepted.

2 Examples

   1.$ AUTHORIZE ADD SMITH/UIC=[200,1]/DEVICE=DUA1:/DIRECTORY=[SMITH]-
         /FLAGS=NODISUSER/PRIVILEGES=(TMPMBX,NETMBX)
     %UAF-I-ADDMSG, user record successfully added
     %UAF-I-RDBADDMSGU, identifier SMITH value [000200,000001] added to rights database

     Adds SMITH, who can then log in with govax --user SMITH.

   2.$ MCR AUTHORIZE
     UAF> MODIFY SMITH/ASTLM=60
     %UAF-I-MDFYMSG, user record(s) updated
     UAF> EXIT
     %UAF-I-DONEMSG, system authorization file modified
     %UAF-I-RDBNOMODS, no modifications made to rights database
